{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And perform yibum with her.</b> The letters mem, shin, and shin serve in building and in拆除; like ״פארות תפאר״ — adorn a branch by pruning its offshoots. <b>וקננו</b> — that is, remove yibum from her, so that she may be yours as a wife."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The Hebrew סתירה literally means 'demolition'; here paired with בנין 'building' as grammatical terms for constructive vs. privative forms. The word וקננו is obscure and translated hyper-literally; the Aramaic-style כלומר introduces the explanation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:50.905351979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}